{% trace-scenario title="Build or buy evaluation infrastructure?" prompt="Your team is shipping production LLM systems and needs quality gates. Braintrust offers specialized evaluation scoring and test case management. Tracify provides evaluation integrated with tracing, cost optimization, and experimentation. Which platform reduces iteration time and production risk?" outcome="Choose based on your observability maturity: evaluation-only platforms for focused quality assessment, or integrated platforms for end-to-end visibility into quality, cost, and performance." /%}

## At a glance

| Dimension | Braintrust | Tracify |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Model** | Specialized evaluation platform | Integrated observability + evaluation |
| **Core strength** | Test case management and scoring | Unified tracing, evaluation, cost, experiments |
| **Evaluation framework** | Advanced, community-built | Production-integrated, native |
| **Tracing** | Integrations available | Native, first-class |
| **Cost tracking** | Manual or third-party integration | Automatic per-call breakdown |
| **Experimentation** | Via external tools | Integrated experiment runner |
| **Setup time** | Hours to days | Minutes to hours |
| **Production readiness** | Strong for evaluation | Complete out-of-box |
| **Best for** | Teams prioritizing eval quality | Teams needing visibility across quality, cost, performance |

### The operating model

**Braintrust** emphasizes *evaluation specialization and flexibility*: test case management, custom scoring functions, dataset versioning, and community-driven evaluator patterns. You own the evaluation workflow and integrate it with your observability stack. **Tracify** emphasizes *integrated production observability*: evaluation is built into tracing, cost tracking, and experimentation from day one. Choose Braintrust when evaluation craftsmanship and dataset quality are your primary concern; choose Tracify when reducing the feedback loop between traces and quality gates matters more than evaluation specialization.

## Opening situation: teams building quality gates

Your team is shipping a multi-agent system in production. You need to:

- **Detect regressions** before users see broken behavior.
- **Understand quality drivers:** Which evaluators matter? What's the cost of each quality improvement?
- **Iterate rapidly:** Measure the impact of prompt changes, model swaps, and routing decisions.
- **Control costs:** Run the best model for each task without overpaying.

This article helps you choose between evaluation-focused infrastructure and integrated observability platforms by showing the real operating differences, naming the cost and effort trade-offs, and identifying when each platform accelerates production confidence.

## Core difference: specialization vs. integration

Braintrust is built for *teams that want evaluation as a first-class discipline*. You define test cases, build or customize evaluators (LLM-as-judge, heuristic, semantic similarity), version datasets, and run batch evaluations. You decide how evaluation fits into your CI/CD and observability stack.

Tracify is built for *teams that want evaluation as part of comprehensive observability*. Evaluation is native to the platform alongside tracing, cost tracking, and experiments. You don't choose between eval and observability—you get both connected by default.

The choice is not primarily about evaluation capability. It is about {% highlight %}whether your observability strategy centers on evaluation quality or production completeness{% /highlight %}. For context on integrated observability architectures, see [Tracify's complete guide to agent observability](/blog/ai-agent-observability-complete-guide).

## Architecture comparison

### Braintrust: evaluation-first, modular

Braintrust's strength is evaluation depth and flexibility. The platform is built around the idea that evaluation is a craft that benefits from specialization and control. You can:

- **Build test datasets** with versioning and fine-grained labeling. Create multiple dataset versions to represent different scenarios (e.g., "edge cases," "high-volume happy path," "multilingual queries").
- **Define custom evaluators:** LLM-as-judge with custom prompts, heuristic scorers, regex patterns, semantic similarity, and even custom Python functions. Evaluators can be composed: run multiple scorers on the same output and aggregate results.
- **Score at scale** across test cases and models. Run batch evaluations across millions of combinations and generate detailed scoring reports with statistical summaries.
- **Integrate with your stack:** Send evaluation results to your CI/CD, monitoring, or external platforms via API. Build custom evaluation workflows that fit your existing tools.
- **Version everything:** Track changes to test cases, evaluators, and scoring logic over time. Understand which evaluator changes caused quality score shifts.
- **Share evaluators within the community:** Braintrust's evaluator marketplace lets you discover, customize, and share evaluation logic with the broader community.

The trade-off: you own the integration between evaluation and other observability signals (tracing, cost, performance metrics). If you need unified dashboards showing evaluation results alongside latency, cost, or other performance metrics, you must build that integration yourself.

### Tracify: integrated, end-to-end

Tracify's strength is production completeness with evaluation built into every level of the observability stack. The platform assumes that in production systems, quality, performance, and cost are inseparable—and your observability should reflect that. You get:

- **Native evaluation.** Define test cases within Tracify or upload from external sources. Test cases are tied to actual production traces, so you can compare evaluation results against real-world performance.
- **Automatic cost analysis.** Per-call cost breakdown by model, provider, region, and route—paired with quality metrics from evaluations. See immediately: "Claude is 40% cheaper than GPT-4 on this task with same quality."
- **Integrated experimentation.** Run A/B tests on prompts, models, routing strategies, and system parameters with automatic quality and cost comparison. Statistical significance testing is built in; no external tools needed.
- **Session tracking.** Multi-turn agent interactions are preserved as sessions with context attached. Evaluation results roll up from individual calls to session-level quality scores, making it easy to spot which conversation steps degrade quality.
- **Unified dashboard.** Traces, evaluation results, cost, and experiments are visualized together. Filter a quality regression and immediately see the associated latency, cost, and model changes.
- **Deployment safety.** Gate deployments on evaluation results: "Don't promote this version unless quality score exceeds threshold."

The trade-off: evaluation is less specialized than Braintrust (you can't write arbitrary Python scorers); SaaS-only with no self-hosting option; you accept Tracify's mental model of evaluation as a first-class observability signal.

## Scenario 1: Building robust evaluation datasets

Your team is shipping an agent that summarizes customer support tickets. The agent must preserve key details, maintain neutral tone, and never omit liability-related information. You need to catch quality regressions before they reach production. Evaluation accuracy is your primary constraint.

**With Braintrust:**
- Create a test dataset of 500 real tickets with reference summaries and fine-grained labels (2-3 days). Tag each summary: "liability_present: yes/no", "tone_appropriate: yes/no", "detail_level: high/medium/low".
- Build a custom evaluator combining multiple scoring methods (1 week of experimentation). Use LLM-as-judge for overall quality, ROUGE for factual completeness, and custom regex patterns to detect missing liability language.
- Version the dataset as quality standards evolve (ongoing, tracked in Braintrust). When legal feedback arrives, create a new dataset version with improved examples.
- Run evaluation in CI/CD before deploying; block if quality score drops below threshold (straightforward Braintrust API integration).
- Customize evaluators for domain-specific rules. Add a scorer that penalizes summaries missing regulatory keywords: "liability," "indemnity," "severability," etc.
- Iterate on scoring logic: if false negatives increase, you can adjust the evaluator weights without touching the test dataset.
- Result: Evaluation is precise and domain-adapted. You control the scoring logic completely. Your evaluators become institutional knowledge—stored in version control, reviewed by domain experts, reused across projects.

**With Tracify:**
- Add API key and instrumentation to your agent (2-3 hours). Every ticket summarization is traced automatically.
- Create 500 test cases in Tracify's dashboard or upload a CSV. Tag each case with metadata: business_unit, difficulty, language.
- Build evaluation using Tracify's native evaluators: LLM-as-judge ("Is this summary complete and neutral?"), ROUGE ("Does the summary overlap with the reference?"), and regex pattern matching ("Does the summary contain liability keywords?").
- Combine evaluators into a quality score using weighted logic: 60% LLM-as-judge, 20% ROUGE, 20% regex. This becomes your quality gate.
- Link evaluation to CI/CD: Tracify automatically blocks deployments if new code drops your quality score below your threshold (e.g., 85%).
- When legal feedback arrives, update your test cases and re-run evaluation. Tracify shows you immediately: "New dataset version shows a 2% quality improvement."
- Bonus: Tracify's dashboard shows the correlation between quality score and production latency and cost. You notice: "Our improved evaluator detects regressions 30 minutes before customers complain."
- Result: Evaluation is production-integrated and reaches velocity fast. You trade customization (no arbitrary Python scorers) for speed. Setup to first quality gate: 4-6 hours.

{% editorial-panel eyebrow="Evaluation maturity" title="Specialized platforms excel when domain knowledge drives scoring." body="Braintrust shines when your evaluation logic is complex, domain-specific, or frequently refined. If you need standard patterns (LLM-as-judge, semantic similarity), Tracify's native evaluators are sufficient and faster to deploy." tone="yellow" /%}

## Scenario 2: Optimizing cost and quality across model choices

Your team runs a multi-model system: Claude (reasoning-heavy tasks), GPT-4o (accuracy-critical tasks), and Mistral (cost-sensitive, high-volume tasks). You need to optimize which model handles each request type without sacrificing quality. Your current setup: 60% GPT-4o, 25% Claude, 15% Mistral. Your goal: reduce spend by 20% while maintaining quality.

**With Braintrust:**
- Instrument each request with the model used, task type, and outcome.
- Create evaluation dataset: 1,000 representative requests across task types with quality labels (correctness, latency, tone).
- Run batch evaluation on each model's output: which model performs best on which task?
- Manual cost tracking: fetch provider pricing from OpenAI and Anthropic docs. Build a spreadsheet: model × task type → cost + quality score.
- Analyze results: "Claude scores 92% on reasoning tasks; GPT-4o scores 94% but costs 3x more."
- Export results to your routing system; hand-build new routing logic: "Use Claude for reasoning, GPT-4o only for complex disambiguations."
- Deploy and monitor manually; if quality drifts, repeat the analysis.
- Result: Evaluation quality is high. Cost optimization is a one-time analysis; ongoing monitoring requires manual work.

**With Tracify:**
- Instrument traces with task type and context (same instrumentation work as Braintrust).
- Tracify automatically fetches real provider pricing for each call. Your dashboard shows: "This month: $12,500 spend, 78% GPT-4o, 15% Claude, 7% Mistral."
- Define evaluation test cases: 1,000 production requests, categorized by task type (reasoning, disambiguation, translation, summarization).
- Create an experiment: "Route reasoning tasks to Claude instead of GPT-4o." Tracify automatically runs evaluation on both versions using your defined quality criteria.
- Experiment results (automatic): Claude version costs 65% less, quality score 91% vs. 94%. The recommendation: "Switch 80% of reasoning to Claude; reserve GPT-4o for edge cases where quality exceeds 98%."
- Deploy the change with a single click. Tracify's quality gates prevent rollout if quality score drops below 90%.
- One week later: Tracify sends you an alert. "Quality on disambiguation tasks dropped to 88%. Likely cause: Claude model update. Recommendation: test routing change." You revert or adjust in minutes.
- Month-end dashboard: spend reduced to $10,200 (18% savings), quality maintained at 91% average.
- Result: Cost optimization is continuous and evidence-led. Experiments are one-click. Deployment is safe. Quality monitoring is automatic.

{% editorial-panel eyebrow="Production velocity" title="Integrated cost and evaluation changes the pace of optimization." body="With Braintrust, cost optimization is a separate analysis problem that requires manual integration of cost data. With Tracify, cost and quality feedback arrive together at every decision point. This difference compounds: teams using Tracify iterate on routing and model selection on a weekly or daily cadence; teams using Braintrust typically optimize quarterly when they have time for custom analysis." tone="yellow" /%}

## Deep comparison: feature by feature

### Evaluation framework

**Braintrust:**
- Custom evaluators with complete control. Write LLM-as-judge prompts with your own scoring rubric. Combine heuristic scorers, regex patterns, semantic similarity, and custom Python functions. Chain evaluators: "Only penalize for bias if the output also contains factual errors."
- Fine-grained test case labeling and metadata. Attach rich context to each test case: difficulty, language, domain, expected output traits. Use this for stratified analysis: "How does our evaluator perform on hard cases vs. easy cases?"
- Batch evaluation runner for millions of combinations. Evaluate 100 test cases × 5 model versions × 3 evaluator versions in one run; get statistical summaries and detailed results.
- Dataset versioning and change tracking. Compare evaluation results across dataset versions. When you add 50 new edge-case examples, see immediately: "New version shows 3% quality decrease; edge cases are being handled poorly."
- Community-driven evaluator library. Share and reuse evaluators with other teams. Discover domain-specific evaluators someone else built.
- No integration with tracing or observability data. Your evaluation results are decoupled from latency, cost, or performance metrics.

**Tracify:**
- Production-ready native evaluators (LLM-as-judge, ROUGE, regex, semantic similarity, custom heuristics). Pre-built and tuned for common patterns. You can customize LLM-as-judge prompts, but you can't write arbitrary Python logic.
- Test case management tied to production traces. Every test case is linked to the traces that produced it. See: "This test case failed; here's the exact span where quality degraded."
- Batch runner integrated with experiments. Run evaluation as part of A/B tests. See results immediately: "Treatment version: 91% quality. Control version: 89% quality. Statistical significance: 95%."
- Evaluation results attached as span metadata. Every production trace carries its evaluation score. This makes evaluation part of your production data, not a separate system.
- Built-in evaluators are production-tested and maintained by Tracify. You don't maintain evaluator code; Tracify updates and fixes evaluators in the platform.
- Full integration with tracing and cost data. Filter by quality, latency, and cost together: "Show me all traces where quality < 85% and cost > $0.05."

**Winner:** Braintrust for evaluation specialization; Tracify for production integration. {% highlight %}Choose Braintrust if evaluator customization and dataset quality are your primary constraints. Choose Tracify if linking evaluation results to traces and costs matters more and you want to ship evaluation infrastructure in days instead of weeks.{% /highlight %}

### Observability integration

**Braintrust:**
- Evaluation focused; tracing via integrations.
- Can consume trace data and apply evaluation.
- Requires external tools to correlate quality with performance, latency, cost.

**Tracify:**
- Evaluation, tracing, cost, and experiments unified.
- Evaluation results are span attributes.
- Quality metrics automatically correlated with latency, cost, model.

**Winner:** Tracify. Observability integration is where the separation becomes stark. Braintrust evaluation is disconnected from production traces.

### Cost tracking and optimization

**Braintrust:**
- Token counting via integrations. You pull token counts from your LLM provider's API and correlate them with Braintrust's evaluation results.
- No native cost breakdown. Braintrust doesn't fetch provider pricing or calculate cost per call. You must manually integrate OpenAI, Anthropic, or cloud pricing data.
- Cost optimization is a manual analysis step. Query Braintrust evaluation results; download cost data from your billing console; use a spreadsheet to analyze cost vs. quality.
- Useful for one-time optimization projects. Not designed for continuous cost monitoring as part of your evaluation workflow.

**Tracify:**
- Automatic cost calculation using real provider pricing. Tracify fetches live pricing from OpenAI, Anthropic, and other providers. Every trace includes the exact cost.
- Per-call cost breakdown by model, provider, region, and route. See: "Claude 3.5 Sonnet: $0.0042 per call; GPT-4o: $0.0090 per call; Mistral Large: $0.0012 per call."
- Cost trending and optimization suggestions. Tracify analyzes your cost distribution and suggests routing changes: "Migrate 30% of task type A to Mistral without quality impact."
- Cost paired with quality metrics in experiments. When you A/B test Claude vs. GPT-4o, Tracify shows both quality and cost in the same view. You see immediately: "Claude is 3x cheaper with equivalent quality."
- Built into deployment gates. Block deployment if cost per request exceeds threshold: "New version is 50% more expensive; requires approval."

**Winner:** Tracify by a wide margin. Cost visibility is automatic, continuous, and integrated with evaluation. Braintrust cost analysis requires manual integration and is not suitable for ongoing monitoring.

### Session and context tracking

**Braintrust:**
- Evaluation is turn-level or conversation-level (you decide scope).
- No native session concept.
- Context correlation is manual.

**Tracify:**
- Native session tracking for multi-turn interactions.
- Evaluation results attached at span and session level.
- Context automatically preserved and correlated.

**Winner:** Tracify. Multi-turn agent interactions are first-class. Braintrust requires external session management.

### Experimentation

**Braintrust:**
- Run evaluation across different prompt versions. Create multiple prompt variants; run batch evaluation on each. Compare evaluation scores manually.
- Score results; analyze manually or export to dashboards. Results are in JSON; you build your own visualization and statistical analysis.
- No native A/B testing framework. Braintrust doesn't tie evaluation to deployment. You can test different prompts, but A/B testing in production requires your own infrastructure.
- Requires external infrastructure for deployment experiments. If you want to deploy treatment and control versions simultaneously and measure quality difference in production, you build this yourself using feature flags and custom logging.
- Useful for offline prompt optimization. Less useful for continuous production experimentation where you want to tie deployment decisions to evaluation results.

**Tracify:**
- Native experiment runner built into the platform. One-click: "Test Claude 3.5 Sonnet vs. GPT-4o on the reasoning task."
- A/B test prompts, models, routing strategies. Tracify automatically routes traffic: 50% to version A, 50% to version B. Both versions are evaluated. Results flow automatically to your dashboard.
- Automatic quality and cost comparison. Tracify shows: "Version A: 91% quality, $0.040/call. Version B: 89% quality, $0.025/call. Winner: Version B (cost savings outweigh quality dip)."
- Statistical significance testing built in. Experiments show confidence intervals. You see: "Version B quality is not significantly different (p > 0.05); cost saving is significant (p < 0.01)."
- Experiments drive deployment decisions. Once experiment concludes, you can promote the winner with a single click. Tracify can tie deployment gates to experiment outcomes.
- Continuous experimentation culture. Because experiments are easy (one-click), teams run more of them. This accelerates learning and iteration velocity.

**Winner:** Tracify decisively. Experiments are first-class infrastructure. Braintrust evaluation can support offline experimentation, but production A/B testing requires external build.

### API maturity and ecosystem

**Braintrust:**
- Strong API for custom evaluation and dataset management.
- Growing community of evaluators and integrations.
- SDK support (Python, Node.js, etc.).

**Tracify:**
- Production API for ingestion, querying, and evaluation.
- TypeScript SDK and Python SDK.
- Integrations with frameworks and monitoring tools.

**Winner:** Tie. Both have mature APIs. Braintrust has a larger community of custom evaluators; Tracify integrations are purpose-built for agents.

## Cost and TCO analysis

Assume a team running 50k LLM calls per month across 10 team members with evaluation as a core quality gate.

### Braintrust

| Item | Cost |
| --- | --- |
| Platform (evaluation, dataset versioning) | $300/month |
| Setup and initial dataset (1 week) | $800 (one-time) |
| Evaluator customization (ongoing) | $1,200/month (0.2 FTE) |
| External cost tracking integration | $500/month (or custom time) |
| Experimentation and routing (custom or third-party) | $500/month |
| **Total monthly** | **$2,500** |
| **Total annual** | **$30,000** |

### Tracify

| Item | Cost |
| --- | --- |
| Platform (tracing, evaluation, cost, experiments) | $800/month |
| Setup and first experiment (2 days) | $300 (one-time) |
| Maintenance (mostly running experiments) | $400/month (0.1 FTE) |
| **Total monthly** | **$1,200** |
| **Total annual** | **$14,400** |

{% highlight %}Braintrust's total cost is lower if you value evaluator customization and don't need cost tracking or experimentation. Tracify's cost is lower if you need complete observability and rapid iteration on model/routing decisions.{% /highlight %}

The hidden cost in Braintrust is integration work: you must build bridges between evaluation results and your CI/CD, cost tracking, and experimentation systems. Tracify's cost is higher per month but lower in total engineering time.

## Trade-offs and boundaries

### Choose Braintrust when:

- **Evaluation craftsmanship is your primary blocker.** You need custom evaluators, fine-grained scoring, or domain-specific quality criteria.
- **You already have observability infrastructure.** Tracing, cost tracking, and experimentation are handled elsewhere; you need evaluation to integrate with them.
- **Your evaluation logic is rapidly evolving.** You want complete control over scoring functions and dataset versioning.
- **Cost of evaluation infrastructure is a constraint.** Braintrust's lower platform cost justifies the integration work.
- **Your team is evaluation-first.** Your primary discipline is ML evaluation, and observability is secondary.

### Choose Tracify when:

- **You want evaluation without integration work.** Traces, quality gates, cost optimization, and experiments are connected by default.
- **Cost visibility is a requirement.** You need per-call cost breakdown without manual integration.
- **Multi-turn agent interactions are central.** Sessions and context preservation matter to your workflow.
- **Iteration velocity is your constraint.** You want to A/B test prompts, models, and routing strategies quickly.
- **Your team is small or distributed.** The operational overhead of integrating multiple tools is a tax on product work.
- **You are building agents, not ML models.** Tracify's paradigm (tracing + evaluation + experiments) maps directly to agent development.

### Hybrid approach: Braintrust for evaluation, Tracify for observability

Some teams use Braintrust for specialized evaluation and Tracify for tracing, cost, and experiments. This approach lets you leverage Braintrust's evaluation depth while using Tracify's observability integration. The trade-off is maintaining two platforms and mapping evaluation results back to traces manually.

### When to reconsider your choice

Your initial decision should not be permanent. Revisit your platform choice if:

- **Evaluation customization becomes a bottleneck.** If Tracify's native evaluators can't express your quality criteria, adding Braintrust is justified. You can run both platforms in parallel during the transition.
- **Integration overhead grows.** If you're spending 20+ hours per month building bridges between Braintrust and your other tools, Tracify's unified approach will likely save engineering time.
- **Experimentation velocity matters more than before.** As you ship agents and need to optimize continuously, Tracify's one-click experiments provide faster iteration than manual Braintrust analysis.
- **Cost tracking becomes critical.** Regulatory, financial, or operational changes may require automatic cost visibility. Tracify provides this; Braintrust requires external integration.
- **Your team size changes.** Small teams (1-3) benefit from Tracify's simplicity; large teams (10+) with dedicated ML engineers may prefer Braintrust's flexibility.

